    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4cf716da-0c14-5f1c-872a-a67f065ee27e" activityNameId="0d7e8fb6-b763-5e2c-b040-915cf6b962bf" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Use, computer, laptop, off mode</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Use, computer, laptop, off mode
The laptop use in the off mode includes the share of the laptop computer production, the energy consumption (use-phase) for the laptop (incl. monitor) and the rail and road transport from factory to user. Energy consumption of laptop computers (use-phase) vary a lot depending on the device looked at. Min.-Max. values are listed;
Synonyms: Notebook, Lifebook; 
UUID: 29e03e5b-41bc-3998-b649-c224b522376e
Describes the use of a laptop computer in the off mode. Calculated per 1 hour of laptop use. Laptop computer life span assumed to be 4 years. Off mode 16.5 hours a day (office use), 240 days a year. UCTE production mix applied for electricity consumption (low voltage).
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: No technology involved, except for the production of the laptop computer, which is described in another dataset.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Manufacturers, literature and own assumptions. 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: International data suitable for Europe.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_29e03e5b-41bc-3998-b649-c224b522376e.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
